-- Query: eb_missing_from_gaia_source (DR4 names)
-- Serves: Question C. Number of long-period eclipsing binaries that have no row in gaia_source. They would be lost
--   by an inner join. Expected 0 in DR3. Limited to long periods because the same join over all 2.2 million rows ran
--   past the archive's 60 second limit for synchronous queries.
-- Names: the draft DR4 data model of 26 Jun 2026. The schema name gaiadr4 is taken from that model's own example
--   query.
-- DR3 stand-in: dr3/eb_missing_from_gaia_source.adql, made from this file by make_standin.py. DR3 tables:
--   gaiadr3.gaia_source, gaiadr3.vari_eclipsing_binary.
-- Last ran without error on the DR3 stand-in: 2026-10-27 (1 rows; results/run_log.tsv).
-- Last ran on DR4: never. The archive has no DR4 until 2 Dec 2026.
-- DR4 columns this query relies on:
--   gaiadr4.gaia_source: source_id
--   gaiadr4.vari_eclipsing_binary: frequency, source_id
-- Lines tagged DR4ONLY have no DR3 equivalent and are dropped from the stand-in.
-- Cannot be tested before release: The DR4 answer. DR4 gaia_source holds only sources with high-quality astrometry
--   and photometry, so it may be above 0. Then position and magnitudes must come from all_source_astrometry and
--   all_source_photometry, which DR3 does not have.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS n_long_period_eb_without_gaia_source_row
FROM gaiadr4.vari_eclipsing_binary AS eb
LEFT OUTER JOIN gaiadr4.gaia_source AS gs
    ON gs.source_id = eb.source_id
WHERE eb.frequency < 0.01
  AND gs.source_id IS NULL
